  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 4, L = 10, P = 24. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[6, 19, 13, 22, 5, 19, 16, 19, 0, 13], [10, 2, 4, 14, 16, 7, 18, 22, 6, 9], [13, 13, 11, 10, 16, 23, 15, 0, 0, 23], [7, 22, 10, 6, 0, 1, 21, 12, 7, 2]], sigma = [6, 9, 8, 4, 3, 7, 0, 5, 2, 1], B = [15, 12, 1, 3, 3, 8, 15, 8, 1, 12].",
